    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver: this is a real route deviation, but the distance it rests on is carried by evidence too weak for me to price it, so the case goes to a human reviewer and no money moves today.\n\nWhat is not in dispute. This is trip TRP-00107, picked up at Blk 226 Ang Mo Kio Ave 3 and set down at One Raffles Place on the night of 18 July 2026. The trip record, the GPS trace and the fare breakdown all carry that identifier on a consistent timeline (requested 21:07:30, started 21:13:40, ended 21:47:40), so the rider has cleared the same-trip burden in POL-RD-08(a).\n\nThe trace is impaired at one level and clean at another, and I must say both. EV-GPS-00107 is down-weighted to 0.30 at the admissibility layer, with issue codes GPS_DRIFT and IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED: a 331.8 m multipath outlier on the final approach into Raffles Place, which also implies an impossible speed. But it is not impaired for policy under POL-RD-07: no gap over 90 s (max 0.0 s), no jump over 500 m (worst 331.8 m) and no sustained interval over 30 s (a steady 10 s). The deviation may therefore still be established on it.\n\nAnd it is established. The trace measures 17.57 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff; the platform's optimal route is 14.00 km (EV-TRIP-00107). The excess is 3.57 km, 25.5% of optimal, over both POL-RD-01 gates (more than 0.8 km and more than 20%). It is not a material deviation (under 8.0 km and under 50%), and the driver's trailing-90-day record (1 flag against 619 trips) shows no repeat pattern, so no POL-RD-06 uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) referral follow.\n\nThe driver's explanation does not exonerate him. POL-RD-03 needs a traffic advisory naming the affected road or segment with an overlapping validity window; there is none — EV-ADVIS-00107-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 — and 'CTE very jam tonight boss' names no advisory and no road segment, so under POL-RD-08 it does not discharge the burden the rider has shifted. Nor is this a rider-requested detour: the only rider chat message challenges the detour rather than requesting one, both waypoint_hint fields are null, and POL-RD-04's corroboration test cannot be run. There was no pickup or dropoff amendment (POL-RD-05), the fare is METERED so POL-RD-11 has no application, and the vehicle was RYDE_X, not a pooled trip (POL-RD-12).\n\nOn the arithmetic that would otherwise follow: reading the surge of 1.35 from EV-FARE-00107 (it lives only there), POL-RD-02 gives a recomputed fare of ((3.80 + 0.75 x 14.00 + 0.28 x 24.0) x 1.35) + 0.80 = 29.177, against a charged total of 36.60, so a refund of 7.423, rounded up to 7.45. POL-RD-09 adds nothing: there are no ERP, toll or surcharge lines to correct.\n\nWhy I cannot issue that refund. POL-GEN-02(2) caps my confidence at the weight of the artifacts that actually carry the deciding fact, and here that fact — the excess distance — is measured from the trace alone, at 0.30. POL-RD-01 bars the trip record's rounded actual_distance_km of 17.6 for the threshold test, and the fare breakdown's distance_charged_km of 17.60 is the same measurement carried across the ledger, not an independent source. The driver's counterparty statement, in which he admits he went by Newton and Kim Seng, is genuine corroboration — it is what satisfies POL-RD-08, which the rider's counters (5 deviation claims in 60 days, 1 substantiated, against a 25.5% excess) bring into play — but a counterparty statement carries no weight_multiplier and so enters neither the minimum nor the maximum of the cap. The chat log (EV-CHAT-00107) records the driver's jam explanation and the rider's challenge, not any measurement of the excess. The cap is therefore 0.30, below the platform-wide floor of 0.70.\n\nResult. POL-RD-10(1) makes the outcome ESCALATE. That is terminal: the disputed amount is held for a human reviewer rather than collected or refunded, and no money moves to either party now. What would settle it is an independent measurement of the distance driven — a second trace, or a corroborating admission about the distance itself — or a traffic advisory covering the CTE that evening, which would let POL-RD-03 be tested."
  },
