    "explanation": "Rider and driver: this concerns trip TRP-00107, Ang Mo Kio to One Raffles Place on the night of 18 July 2026, charged at SGD 36.60. I find the driver did leave the optimal route and had no valid excuse for it; the rider is refunded SGD 7.45 and the balance of the charge stands.\n\nTHE DEVIATION. POL-RD-01 sets the test and names its own governing field: gps_trace.trace_distance_km. On EV-GPS-00107 that is 17.57 km; the platform's optimal route on EV-TRIP-00107 is 14.00 km. The excess is 3.57 km, or 25.5% of optimal, clearing both establishment limbs (over 0.8 km and over 20%). I have deliberately not used trip_record.actual_distance_km of 17.6, which POL-RD-01 forbids as a rounded copy. The excess is under both materiality gates (8.0 km and 50%), so this is an ordinary, non-MATERIAL deviation and no full-refund uplift arises.\n\nTHE GPS TRACE — IMPAIRED, BUT USABLE. I name EV-GPS-00107 as impaired at weight 0.30, issue codes GPS_DRIFT and IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED: a 331.8 m multipath jump on the final approach into Raffles Place implying impossible speeds. But POL-RD-07 uses different, looser thresholds, and for policy purposes the trace is clean — no gap over 90 s (largest 0.0 s), no jump over 500 m (worst 331.8 m), no sustained interval over 30 s (a steady 10 s). The two are not the same thing and I say both: the trace is schema-impaired yet policy-usable, and the deviation may be established on it. The 0.30 weight bites on my confidence only, under POL-GEN-02(2); it does not trigger POL-RD-10(3).\n\nINDEPENDENCE AND CONFIDENCE. The fact that the driver left the corridor does not rest on the trace alone. It is carried independently by the contemporaneous in-trip chat, EV-CHAT-00107 (weight 1.0), in which the rider asks 'why exit at whitley? CTE goes straight down what' and the driver answers 'cte very jam tonight boss' without denying the exit; and it is admitted in the driver's own statement ('I went by Newton and Kim Seng to avoid it'). Because a weight-1.0 artifact carries the same fact independently of the impaired trace, the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is the maximum of the independent carriers, 1.0 — not the trace's 0.30 — and my confidence is 0.85.\n\nTHE RIDER'S CORROBORATION DUTY. Under POL-RD-08 (deviation_claims_60d 5 against deviation_claims_60d_substantiated 1, on a claim under 30%) the rider needed support beyond the trace. It is met: the driver's counterparty statement admits the route, which POL-RD-07(ii) names as an independent source. That factor is not used to deny a claim that is otherwise proven.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S TRAFFIC EXCUSE. The driver says the CTE was jammed. POL-RD-03 exonerates only where a traffic_advisory names a road the optimal route uses, with a window covering the time. There is none: EV-ADVIS-00107-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) and no congestion advisory was issued. A general assertion that traffic was bad, with no advisory to point to, does not discharge the driver's burden (POL-RD-08). None of the 3.57 km is set aside on this ground.\n\nNO RIDER-REQUESTED DETOUR. POL-RD-04 is unavailable. Its test needs a waypoint_hint the vehicle passes within 200 m of; both chat messages carry waypoint_hint null, and the rider's message challenges the route rather than requesting it. On the clause's own terms the corroboration test cannot be run, and I record that it could not be run.\n\nTHE REFUND. EV-FARE-00107 shows fare_model METERED, so POL-RD-02 governs and POL-RD-11 has no application. The surge multiplier is read from EV-FARE-00107, where it is 1.35 — not from the trip record, which does not carry the field. On separate lines: charged_total SGD 36.60; recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 14.00 + 0.28 x 24.0) x 1.35) + 0.80 = SGD 29.177 (not rounded at any intermediate step); refund = 36.60 - 29.177 = SGD 7.423, rounded up to SGD 7.45. That is 20.3% of the charge — above the SGD 0.50 de minimis, so not NO_ACTION, and far below the 90% that would make it a full refund. POL-RD-09 adds nothing: there are no ERP or toll lines and no airport surcharge, so there is no pass-through correction to make and nothing is double-counted.\n\nPROFILES. The repeat-deviation check under POL-RD-06 shows no pattern (deviation_flags_90d 1 against completed_trips_90d 619), so there is no full-refund uplift and no conduct referral. The remaining profile counters on both sides — rating, cancellation_rate, prior_disputes_filed, prior_disputes_upheld, prior_no_show_flags, prior_deviation_flags, acceptance_rate and the rest — are context only under POL-GEN-01 and have carried no finding about this trip.\n\nOUTCOME: PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 7.45 to the rider. No driver compensation is due (the driver was billed for 17.60 km against a 17.57 km trace, so there is no unbilled distance). No clause produces a referral, so no referral is made."
  },
